ype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"---\ninstruments: BTC, ETH, BNB\n---\nWhen price makes a new high while RSI makes a lower high, or a new low while RSI makes a higher low, does this divergence predict that price will turn?\n\n**Why it could predict a turn (my reasoning, not from a source):** The divergence means the new extreme was reached with smaller, less frequent moves. That suggests fewer participants are still pushing the trend. Once the last trend-chasers are in, no one is left to extend it, and price falls back.\n\n**Why it could fail:** In crypto, strong trends often slow down without reversing. Momentum can fade in a range or a pause, and the trend can then resume.\n\n**What would show it wrong:** After divergences, price does not turn against the prior trend more often or further than it does after comparable new highs or lows without divergence.\n\nshort-name: rsi-divergence-predicts-reversal\nindex-line: Does a divergence between price extremes and RSI extremes predict a turn in price? [instruments: BTC, ETH, BNB]","ttft_ms":5963,"type":"result","duration_ms":11541,"uuid":"ceeddac5-c89b-4993-b831-282520f00ae0","ttft_stream_ms":970,"time_to_request_ms":132,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":0,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":61,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":1,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":25,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":99,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":171,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":99,"process_rss_mib_result":179,"process_anon_mib_result":103,"process_peak_rss_mib":179,"process_cpu_ms_turn":459,"process_wall_ms_